<title>UK: Less than 1,000 UK Ford jobs to go -union.</title>
<headline>Less than 1,000 UK Ford jobs to go -union.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>An agreement reached between unions and Ford Motor Co means fewer than 1,000 jobs are to go at Ford's Halewood, Merseyside plant, Larry Brooke of the MSF union told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>Brooke was speaking before a news conference called to announce the agreement.</p>
<p>Unions had said 1,300 jobs were to go at Halewood under Ford's orginal plans to cut costs and produce a new Escort model in continental Europe.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
